# Full path, not `||powershell`: the alias form resolves only against a published
# TSAppAllowList\Applications entry, and outside the matrix's Enforce window there is none --
# the first dry run (2026-09-06 05:08) came back RAIL_EXEC_E_FILE_NOT_FOUND and the server
# dropped the session. With unlisted programs allowed (fDisabledAllowList=1, the restored state)
# the full path launches; while the list is enforced without powershell it will be refused as
# RAIL_EXEC_E_NOT_IN_ALLOWLIST -- either answer is a result, not a hang.
PROGRAM='C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe'
CMDARGS='-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\tsclient\lab\server-snapshot.ps1'
# Bound. Measured: dry runs 3-7 (2026-09-06) went from relay launch to the report's RESULT line in
# under 45 s each, reading 42 RDS-related channels at up to 2500 events apiece (the largest held
# 1891-1952 records, i.e. scanned whole), one `Get-WinEvent -ListProvider *` (the only unbounded
# call: 1359 providers), six registry keys and about a dozen bounded System-log queries. 240 s is
# a >5x margin over that; the report is checkpointed at start and after every channel, so a
# timeout still leaves every finished section on the drive.
#
# OPERATOR STEP before every launch: remove the previous report, e.g.
#   rm -f .build/lab-runtime/share/server-snapshot-out.txt
# The script overwrites it as its first act, but a job the host refuses before the script starts
# (RAIL exec error, connection failure) leaves the previous run's complete report -- RESULT: DONE
# included -- on the drive, indistinguishable from a fresh success except by its ReadAtUtc line.
# run-scenario.sh deliberately never removes host-written *-out.txt (see stage_share).
TIMEOUT=240
